    {
      "id": "b7c3d1e0-0000-4a00-9000-000000000003",
      "name": "Search job posts",
      "type": "@apify/n8n-nodes-apify.apify",
      "position": [
        480,
        520
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "memory": 1024,
        "actorId": "dami_studio~linkedin-jobs-scraper",
        "timeout": 300,
        "resource": "Actors",
        "operation": "Run actor and get dataset",
        "customBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({ searchQueries: $json.searchQueries.split(',').map(s => s.trim()), locations: $json.locations.split(',').map(s => s.trim()), datePosted: 'pastWeek', maxItems: $json.maxItems }) }}",
        "maxTotalChargeUsd": 1
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "b7c3d1e0-0000-4a00-9000-000000000005",
      "name": "Keep readable posts",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.filter",
      "position": [
        720,
        520
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "version": 3,
            "leftValue": "",
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "typeValidation": "loose"
          },
          "combinator": "and",
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "b7c3d1e0-0000-4a00-9+1234567890",
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true",
                "singleValue": true
              },
              "leftValue": "={{ !!$json.company && !!($json.description || $json.title) }}",
              "rightValue": ""
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 2.3
    },
    {
      "id": "b7c3d1e0-0000-4a00-9000-000000000006",
      "name": "Only jobs not read yet",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.removeDuplicates",
      "position": [
        960,
        520
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {
          "scope": "node",
          "historySize": 100000
        },
        "operation": "removeItemsSeenInPreviousExecutions",
        "dedupeValue": "={{ $json.jobId || $json.url }}"
      },
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "b7c3d1e0-0000-4a00-9000-000000000007",
      "name": "Read the buying signal",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "position": [
        1200,
        520
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "text": "=Someone sells: {{ $('Roles that signal a buyer').item.json.sell }}\n\nRead one job post and say what the hire implies the company is about to do.\n\nCompany: {{ $json.company }}\nRole: {{ $json.title }}\nLocation: {{ $json.location || 'unknown' }}\nDescription: {{ ($json.description || '').toString().slice(0, 3000) }}\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON, no code fence, with these keys:\n\"building\": what this hire suggests the company is standing up or scaling, in one sentence.\n\"implied_need\": what they will plausibly need to buy because of it, or \"no clear implication\" - use that rather than reaching.\n\"timing\": \"now\", \"next quarter\" or \"unknown\", and say what in the post tells you.\n\"relevance\": 1 to 5 for how well this maps to what the seller offers.",
        "promptType": "define"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.9
    },
    {
      "id": "gate-relevance",
      "name": "Strong enough to act on?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "position": [
        1460,
        520
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "version": 2,
            "leftValue": "",
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "typeValidation": "loose"
          },
          "combinator": "and",
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "gate-1",
              "operator": {
                "type": "number",
                "operation": "gte"
              },
              "leftValue": "={{ JSON.parse($json.text).relevance }}",
              "rightValue": "={{ $('Roles that signal a buyer').first().json.minRelevance }}"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 2.2
    },
    {
      "id": "b7c3d1e0-0000-4a00-9000-000000000008",
      "name": "OpenAI chat model",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatOpenAi",
      "position": [
        1200,
        720
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "model": {
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "gpt-5-mini"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "b7c3d1e0-0000-4a00-9000-000000000009",
      "name": "Add the signal to Notion",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.notion",
      "position": [
        1720,
        520
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "title": "={{ $('Only jobs not read yet').item.json.company }}",
        "options": {},
        "resource": "databasePage",
        "operation": "create",
        "databaseId": {
          "mode": "list",
          "value": ""
        },
        "propertiesUi": {
          "propertyValues": [
            {
              "key": "Role|rich_text",
              "textContent": "={{ $('Only jobs not read yet').item.json.title }}"
            },
            {
              "key": "Building|rich_text",
              "textContent": "={{ JSON.parse($json.text).building }}"
            },
            {
              "key": "Implied need|rich_text",
              "textContent": "={{ JSON.parse($json.text).implied_need }}"
            },
            {
              "key": "Timing|rich_text",
              "textContent": "={{ JSON.parse($json.text).timing }}"
            },
            {
              "key": "Relevance|rich_text",
              "textContent": "={{ JSON.parse($json.text).relevance }}"
            },
            {
              "key": "Link|rich_text",
              "textContent": "={{ $('Only jobs not read yet').item.json.url }}"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 2.2
    },
    {
      "id": "b7c3d1e0-0000-4a00-9000-000000000010",
      "name": "Sticky Note overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -640,
        40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 520,
        "height": 1820,
        "content": "## Turn LinkedIn job posts into sales buying signals with Apify, OpenAI and Notion\n\nA company hiring for a role is telling you what it is about to spend money on. This reads job posts, scores how well each hire maps to what you sell, and files only the ones worth acting on.\n\n**Who is this for?**\nB2B sellers who know hiring is a buying signal and have no way to watch it at scale.\n\n**What problem is this workflow solving?**\nJob posts are the most public statement of intent a company makes, and nobody in sales reads them because they are written for candidates. The inference is one step away and nobody has time to make it a hundred times.\n\n**What this workflow does**\n- Runs your job searches and keeps posts with a company and a description to read.\n- Skips anything already read in a previous run.\n- Asks a model what the hire implies and how well it maps to what you sell.\n- Sends anything at or above your relevance threshold to Notion, and drops the rest.\n\n**Setup**\n1. Add an Apify, an OpenAI and a Notion credential.\n2. Pick your Notion database in the last node.\n3. Set the roles, locations and what you sell in \"Roles that signal a buyer\".\n4. Set `minRelevance`. 4 keeps it tight, 3 gives you more to sift.\n\n**Requirements**\nAn Apify account and API token, an OpenAI API key, and a Notion database you can add pages to — or no Notion at all, if you plug in one of the optional nodes instead.\n\n**How to customize this workflow to your needs**\n\nFour nodes sit under the main row, wired to nothing on purpose. Drag a connection into the ones you want and delete the rest:\n\n- **Slack** — ping a channel when a strong signal lands.\n- **Google Sheets** — wire it to the gate's *false* output and keep the weak signals as a backlog instead of binning them.\n- **Gmail** — mail it to yourself instead of opening Notion.\n- **HTTP Request** — post the signal as JSON into your own CRM.\n\n**Good to know**\nA job post proves intent to hire, not budget for anything else. The model is told to say \"no clear implication\" rather than invent one, and it does — expect the gate to drop most of what the search returns. That is it working, not the search failing."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
